    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (which regenerates `OwnerDto`). `telephone` in `OwnerFields` stays as raw E.164.\n\n2. **`TelephoneE164.java`** \u2014 added a `toDisplay(String e164)` helper that recognises the country code from the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` table, then emits the country code, a space, and the national digits grouped in threes (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). Values not in E.164 form or with an unknown country code are returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping populating `telephoneDisplay` from `TelephoneE164.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe target test asserts `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`, and `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
